    "lawCode": "Add §3-a, Chap 607 of 2004",
    "lawSection": "",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5506\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend chapter 607 of the laws of 2004, relating to\nauthorizing the town of Marcellus to extend the Marcellus fire\nprotection district into the village of Marcellus, in relation to\nauthorizing the town to purchase the fire barn and equipment located\nin the village of Marcellus\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nThis bill authorizes the Town of Marcellus to extend the Marcellus\nfire protection district into the Village of Marcellus, in relation to\nauthorizing the town to purchase the fire barn and equipment located\nin the Village of Marcellus.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nThis bill will amend Chapter 607 of the laws of 2004, relating to\nauthorizing the Town of Marcellus to purchase, hold title and maintain\nthe fire barn facility and equipment in the fire protection district\nin the Village of Marcellus.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nIn 2004, the Town of Marcellus established a fire protection district.\nIn the same year, the town requested of the State Legislature to pass\nlegislation to allow the Town of Marcellus to extend its fire\nprotection to include the Village of Marcellus. The Marcellus\nVolunteer Fire Department's barn is currently in the Village of\nMarcellus. The Town has been leasing the Department's fire barn and\nequipment from the Village. The town essentially, is reimbursing the\nvillage for the majority of the cost to operate the fire department\nand bond payments for the construction of the fire barn, previously\nbonded by the village. Currently, approximately eighty percent of the\nFire Department's budget is paid by Town residents. The Town and\nVillage both desire to transfer ownership of the fire barn to the\nTown.\n\nThis bill will allow the Town of Marcellus to purchase, hold title to\nand maintain the fire barn facility and equipment in the fire\nprotection district in the Village of Marcellus.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
