    "lawCode": "Add §3-a, Chap 607 of 2004",
    "lawSection": "Onondaga County",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5506A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend chapter 607 of the laws of 2004, relating to\nauthorizing the town of Marcellus to extend the Marcellus fire\nprotection district into the village of Marcellus, in relation to\nauthorizing the town to purchase the fire barn and equipment located\nin the village of Marcellus\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nThis bill authorizes the town of Marcellus to extend the Marcellus\nFire protection district into the village of Marcellus, in relation to\nauthorizing the town to purchase the fire barn and equipment located\noutside the Village of the Marcellus.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nThis bill will amend Chapter 607 of the laws of 2004, relating to\nauthorizing the town of Marcellus to purchase, hold title to and\nmaintain the fire barn facility and equipment in the fire protection\ndistrict outside the Village of Marcellus.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nIn 2004, the Town of Marcellus established a fire protection district.\nIn the same year, the Town requested that the State Legislature pass\nlegislation to allow the Town of Marcellus to extend its fire\nprotection district to include the Village of Marcellus. The Marcellus\nVolunteer Fire Department's barn currently resides outside the Village\nof Marcellus. The Town has been leasing the Department's fire barn and\nequipment from the Village. The Town is reimbursing the village for\nthe majority of the cost to operate the fire department and bond\npayments for the construction of the fire barn, previously bonded by\nthe Village. Currently, approximately eighty percent of the Fire\nDepartment's budget is paid by Town residents. The Town and Village\nboth desire to transfer ownership of the fire barn to the Town.\n\nThis bill will allow the town of Marcellus to purchase, hold title to\nand maintain the fire barn facility and equipment in the fire\nprotection district outside the Village of Marcellus.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to state.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
